The BAER dataset and derived outputs in this repository are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

Rationale: BAER is derived from US federal and state government records,
which are not subject to copyright in the United States, and from the NIH
Dietary Supplement Label Database, which is itself released under CC0. A more
restrictive licence on the derived record would be inconsistent with the
status of its inputs.

Upstream terms that still apply:
  DSLD                CC0 1.0
  openFDA             US Government work; see https://open.fda.gov/terms/
  FDA warning letters US Government work
  CA AG Prop 65       California public record
  GBIF backbone       CC BY 4.0 -- attribute GBIF when redistributing the
                      taxonomic annotations

Attribution is appreciated but not required for BAER itself; GBIF requires it
for the taxonomy.
